  "evidence": "Mentions a £400bn National Transformation Fund with a £250bn Green Transformation Fund; public ownership of rail, buses, energy and water; free full‑fibre broadband by 2030 via a public provider; £10 Real Living Wage and 32‑hour week; abolish tuition fees; bring academies/free schools under local oversight; end Right to Buy; abolish the House of Lords and replace with an elected Senate; recognise Palestine; retain NATO/2% defence and renew the nuclear deterrent; Brexit plan of a new customs‑union‑based deal put to a confirmatory referendum alongside remain within six months. These are hallmark planks of the UK Labour Party’s 2019 general election manifesto.",
